# SteelOS kernel command-line hardening fragment.
#
# Paired with CMDLINE_BASELINE in tools/steel-check/src/checks/kernel.rs; a unit
# test fails the build if they drift apart.
#
# On an image deployment these parameters live inside the signed UKI, so they
# cannot be edited without invalidating the signature. On a plain-Arch install
# (Phase 0) this file is documentation: append it to your bootloader entry by
# hand. steel-check reports the difference as a warning rather than a failure,
# because the package cannot apply it for you.
#
# Deliberately NOT included here, and why:
#
#   lockdown=confidentiality    Applied by steel-boot on image deployments. On a
#                               mutable Arch install it breaks hibernation and
#                               any locally-built module, so it is opt-in via
#                               `steel-harden lockdown on`.
#   module.sig_enforce=1        Only safe once modules are built and signed at
#                               image build time. Setting it on a DKMS system
#                               makes the machine unbootable after the next
#                               kernel update.
#   mitigations=auto,nosmt      Costs roughly a third of the machine's
#                               throughput. `steel-harden smt off` for users who
#                               want it.
#   intel_iommu=on / amd_iommu  Vendor-specific; steel-boot picks the right one
#                               from the detected CPU.

slab_nomerge init_on_alloc=1 init_on_free=1 page_alloc.shuffle=1
randomize_kstack_offset=on vsyscall=none debugfs=off mitigations=auto
